# src/apps/daemon/internal/foundation/config

## Purpose
Daemon configuration schemas, defaults, templates, and config normalization; configuration knowledge is centralized here rather than duplicated in callers.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `foundation` (rank 0; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (14): `atomic_file.go`, `atomic_file_test.go`, `config.go`, `config_secret_refs_test.go`, `defaults.go`, `quarantine.go`, `quarantine_test.go`, `randmap_egress.go`, `randmap_egress_test.go`, `revision_test.go`, `tpm_lifecycle.go`, `tpm_lifecycle_test.go` …

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `config`.
- Notable exported surface: `AppendError`, `CaptchaSolverConfig`, `Config`, `DDNSConfig`, `DecoyTrafficConfig`, `DefaultConfig`, `DefaultDBPath`, `DefaultLogLevel`, `DefaultPluginsDir`, `DefaultServerAddr` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/crypto`, `internal/foundation/secrets`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/runtime/proxy`.

## Invariants
- `foundation` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
